From 2737b837dbe6179add4bb3d8392086f629133683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 04:04:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: protected-win learns a symbols class - a
 registered kernel entry point must have a DEFINITION, not a mention (WI-1700)

R13's b10819 merge deleted the body of ggml_cuda_moe_cache_mmv_fused from ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu while
its .cuh declaration and its moe-cache.cu caller survived; protected-win validate reported 41/41
anchors healthy and the fork stopped linking on CUDA (WI-1699). An anchor proves a STRING survives;
this adds the class that proves a BODY does.

- protected-wins.json entries may carry symbols: {file: [names]}. validate (and therefore check
  and bump leg 1b) fails closed when a name has no definition-shaped match in that file - name,
  parameter list, then '{' after optional qualifiers, or an explicit template instantiation.
  A declaration ending in ';', a call site, or a [[host_name()]] attribute never satisfies it.
- on a miss the problem names the symbol, the file, every surviving source mention, and the last
  commit that touched the definition (git log -S, scope widened file -> dir -> tree, because a
  single-file pathspec hides the merge under history simplification - CHECKED on 697027562).
- seed: 32 symbols across 12 entries (Vulkan, CUDA, Metal, ggml-cpu; SYCL carries no ArifiLabs
  kernel). ggml_cuda_moe_cache_mmv_fused is seeded on purpose and is RED on this branch tip -
  that RED is the WI-1699 proof, banked in lane-evidence wi1700-protected-win-symbols/.
- tests: 39 -> 43 (RED with declaration+caller kept, GREEN when the body returns, the shapes this
  fork uses, malformed field refuses). UPDATE-RUNBOOK 4.1c step 0/1 name the class.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
